Subject: [PATCH v1 00/22] arm64: dts: qcom: add Samsung Galaxy A52 4G (a52q, SM7125)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the device tree for the Samsung Galaxy A52 4G (a52q), an SM7125
(SC7180-family) phone, plus the SC7180 SoC DT additions it relies on
(CCI/CAMSS nodes, GPI DMA, LPASS audio macros/LPI TLMM).

This is the capstone of the a52q bring-up and depends on the driver and
binding series sent separately (regulator s2mpb03, power-supply/typec
sm5714, nfc s3fwrn5, input fts5cu56a, drm panel s6e3fc3, drm/msm A618,
ASoC tas2562, soc/qcom smp2p + pd-mapper, firmware tzmem, and the media
camss/sensor series). See SERIES.md.

NOTE: four DT commits (sc7180 CCI/CAMSS, sc7180 GPI DMA, a52q NFC, and
'allow keys to wake the device') currently lack Signed-off-by lines; the
author must add them before sending.

Based on v7.3-rc5. On-device verification pending.

Erikas Bitovtas (2):
  dt-bindings: arm: qcom: Document Samsung Galaxy A52/A72
  arm64: dts: qcom: sm7125-samsung: add initial device tree

